A :REGION whose body is not SSL: JSON with braces and colons, an HTML
fragment with quotes, and lines that look like SSL keywords and comments
but have no semicolons. The region body is stored text read by
GetRegion(), a multi-line token the formatter preserves byte for byte
(feature.formatting A11); no diagnostics may come from inside it.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Template;
	:RETURN GetRegion("Payload");
:ENDPROC;

:REGION Payload;
{
  "sample": {"id": 42, "status": "P"},
  "tags": ["a", "b"]
}
<div class="note">Don't :IF this "works"</div>
:IF looks like code
/* not a comment
    deeply   indented    text
:ENDREGION;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Template;
	:RETURN GetRegion("Payload");
:ENDPROC;

:REGION Payload;
{
  "sample": {"id": 42, "status": "P"},
  "tags": ["a", "b"]
}
<div class="note">Don't :IF this "works"</div>
